Remove the "Ask Gemini" entry from the three-dot menu.

Aerium ships no Google AI integration, and stock upstream already keeps most
Google-integration menu items out of non-Chrome-branded builds by construction
elsewhere in this file. Glic is the exception: AppMenuModel adds it purely
based on glic::GlicEnabling::IsEnabledForProfile(), a runtime eligibility
check with no branding gate, so it can appear in an Aerium build without any
patch telling it to.

The block is removed outright rather than gated behind a flag, matching the
"nothing installed unless you ask" stance the rest of this browser takes with
Google-provided features. IDC_OPEN_GLIC's ExecuteCommand() case earlier in
this file is unreachable once nothing ever adds the menu item, which is fine:
it costs nothing left in place, and removing it too would be touching code
this patch has no reason to.

Generated by applying the change to the real file at the 152.0.7977.82 tag and
diffing, not written by hand.

